      "summaries": {
        "en": "SpiderFoot is an open-source OSINT automation tool that helps security professionals map attack surfaces and gather threat intelligence. It integrates over 200 modules to collect data from public sources like DNS, social media, and dark web forums, correlating findings to reveal hidden connections. You can use it via CLI or web UI to investigate domains, IPs, or email addresses, making it ideal for reconnaissance, penetration testing, and continuous security monitoring.",
        "zh": "SpiderFoot 是一款开源 OSINT 自动化工具，专为威胁情报和攻击面测绘设计。它通过 200 多个模块从 DNS、社交媒体、暗网论坛等公开来源收集数据，并自动关联分析，揭示隐藏的实体关系。技术亮点在于模块化架构和灵活的扫描策略，用户可自定义工作流。你可以通过命令行或 Web 界面快速扫描域名、IP 或邮箱，适用于渗透测试、红队侦察和持续安全监控。无需复杂配置，即可生成可视化报告，帮助安全团队发现暴露面并提前防御。",
        "es": "SpiderFoot is an open-source OSINT automation tool that helps security professionals map attack surfaces and gather threat intelligence. It integrates over 200 modules to collect data from public sources like DNS, social media, and dark web forums, correlating findings to reveal hidden connections. You can use it via CLI or web UI to investigate domains, IPs, or email addresses, making it ideal for reconnaissance, penetration testing, and continuous security monitoring.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "spiderfoot stands out for attacksurface, cti, and cybersecurity in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "SpiderFoot is an open-source OSINT automation tool that helps security professionals map attack surfaces and gather threat intelligence. It integrates over 200 modules to collect data from public sources like DNS, social media, and dark web forums, correlating findings to reveal hidden connections. You can use it via CLI or web UI to investigate domains, IPs, or email addresses, making it ideal for reconnaissance, penetration testing, and continuous security monitoring.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/smicallef/spiderfoot for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
